cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the released measurement tables, please cite the paper and this repository."
title: "Where Should the Keep-Mask Come From? Code, measurement tables and artefact bundle"
abstract: >-
  Analysis code and measurement tables for a controlled study of preservation-mask sources in
  training-free video editing. The repository compares an external segmentation mask, a
  self-attention-derived identity gate, and a parameter-free centred prior under an otherwise
  identical pipeline, and ships a GPU-free script that recomputes every reported number.
version: 1.5
date-released: "2026-11-21"
license: MIT
